"8814f190336785b472c6668ca2f5efe754d3b82e": {
"body": "{\"parse\":{\"title\":\"Amstel\",\"pageid\":715790,\"redirects\":[],\"wikitext\":\"{{Short description|River in North Holland, the Netherlands}}\\n{{About|the Dutch river|the brewery|Amstel Brewery}}\\n{{Infobox river\\n| name                = Amstel\\n| native_name         = \\n| native_name_lang    = \\n| other_name          = \\n| etymology           = \\n<!---------------------- IMAGE & MAP -->\\n| image               = Amsterdam Amstel 12.jpg\\n| image_size          = 250px\\n| image_caption       = The Amstel in city center of Amsterdam with the [[Stopera]] (center) and [[H'ART Museum]] (right)\\n| map                 = Location Amstel with Drechtkanaal.PNG\\n| map_size            = 250px\\n| map_caption         = Location of the Amstel in dark blue\\n| pushpin_map         = \\n| pushpin_map_size    = \\n| pushpin_caption     = \\n<!---------------------- LOCATION -->\\n| subdivision_type1   = Country\\n| subdivision_name1   = [[Netherlands]]\\n| subdivision_type2   = Province\\n| subdivision_name2   = [[North Holland]], [[South Holland]], [[Utrecht (province)|Utrecht]]\\n| subdivision_type3   = Water board\\n| subdivision_name3   = [[Water board (Netherlands)#List of water boards|Amstel, Gooi en Vecht]]\\n| subdivision_type4   = Municipalities\\n| subdivision_name4   = [[Nieuwkoop]], [[Uithoorn]], [[De Ronde Venen]], [[Amstelveen]], [[Ouder-Amstel]], [[Amsterdam]]\\n| subdivision_type5   = \\n| subdivision_name5   = \\n<!---------------------- PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTICS -->\\n| length              = {{convert|31|km|mi|abbr=on}}\\n| width_min           = \\n| width_avg           = \\n| width_max           = \\n| depth_min           = \\n| depth_avg           = \\n| depth_max           = \\n| discharge1_location = \\n| discharge1_min      = \\n| discharge1_avg      = \\n| discharge1_max      = \\n<!---------------------- BASIN FEATURES -->\\n| source1             = [[Aarkanaal]] / [[Drecht]]\\n| source1_location    = [[Nieuwveen]], [[South Holland]]\\n| source1_coordinates = {{coord|52|12|24|N|4|44|05|E|display=inline}}\\n| source1_elevation   = \\n| mouth               = [[IJ (Amsterdam)|IJ]]\\n| mouth_location      = [[Amsterdam]], [[North Holland]]\\n| mouth_coordinates   = {{coord|52|22|08|N|4|53|33|E|display=inline}}\\n| mouth_elevation     = \\n| progression         = \\n| river_system        = \\n| basin_size          = \\n| tributaries_left    = \\n| tributaries_right   = \\n| custom_label        = \\n| custom_data         = \\n| extra               = \\n}}\\n\\nThe '''Amstel''' ({{IPA|nl|ˈɑmstəl|lang|Nl-Amstel.ogg}}) is a river in the province of [[North Holland]] in the [[Netherlands]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://m.theindependentbd.com//magazine/details/7145/Amsterdam-%E2%80%93-Venice-of-the-North|title=Amsterdam {{•}} Venice of the North|website=theindependentbd.com|publisher=[[The Independent]]|first=Shamim|last=Ahmed|access-date=15 June 2022|date=10 July 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220615062341/https://m.theindependentbd.com//magazine/details/7145/Amsterdam-%E2%80%93-Venice-of-the-North|archive-date=15 June 2022}}</ref> It flows from the Aarkanaal and Drecht in [[Nieuwveen]] northwards, passing [[Uithoorn]], [[Amstelveen]], and [[Ouderkerk aan de Amstel]], to the [[IJ (Amsterdam)|IJ]] in [[Amsterdam]], to which the river gives its name. Annually, the river is the location of the [[Liberation Day (Netherlands)|Liberation Day]] concert, [[Head of the River Amstel]] rowing match, and the [[Amsterdam Gay Pride]] boat parade.\"}}",
"status": 200,
"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php?action=parse&page=Amstel&prop=wikitext&section=0&redirects=1&format=json&formatversion=2"
},
